#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186135006} :activity/id #uuid "e6580470-6b81-57e7-bf68-123e2ad0a485" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050659 :topic/id #uuid "5cfd2722-99a9-5eb4-adb4-6386be397f59" :topic/math-academy-id 2218} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134893 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186135147 :tutorial/content "As we mentioned earlier, rigid motions are **distance-preserving**.\n\nFor example, if a rigid motion maps $\\triangle ABC$ to $\\triangle A'B'C'$, then the corresponding sides of the triangles must be congruent:\n\n$$\nAB = A'B', \\qquad AC = A'C', \\qquad BC = B'C'\n$$\n\nIn addition, rigid motions are **angle-preserving**, which means that the corresponding angles of the triangles must be congruent as well:\n\n$$\nm\\angle A = m\\angle A', \\qquad m\\angle B = m\\angle B', \\qquad m\\angle C = m\\angle C'\n$$\n\nSince all of the corresponding sides and angles are congruent, the triangles are congruent, and we write\n\n$$\n\\triangle ABC \\cong \\triangle A'B'C'\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "4514dc0f-bb78-52d9-a728-8a09f7cbf667" :tutorial/math-academy-id 6157 :tutorial/title "Further Properties of Rigid Motions"} :step/id #uuid "6caa4091-01f6-57a9-8303-9c7ac2687088" :step/math-academy-id 37342 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186135007}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134894 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186135148 :tutorial/content "So, remember, there are *only three* types of rigid motions:\n\n- Translations\n- Rotations\n- Reflections\n\nThere are two properties of rigid motions we need to know:\n\n- *A rigid motion maps every polygon to a congruent polygon.*\n- *For any pair of congruent polygons, there exists a rigid motion that maps one polygon onto another.*\n\nConsider the diagram below. Let's use the concept of rigid motions to explain why $\\mathcal{P}$ and $\\mathcal{Q}$ are congruent.\n\n![](images/04/0487c9bb2a640a44e9ee67830937db4272c97f4a5f5101e43e3dcf3edd6c3a1c.png)\n\nNotice that $\\mathcal{Q}$ is the image of $\\mathcal{P}$ under the action of reflection in the $x$-axis.\n\n![](images/18/183b182e26df36c6cfe6a9d682e0f3b000bff40ce7d405255a0abfee8529a946.png)\n\nSince $\\mathcal P$ is mapped to $\\mathcal Q$ under a rigid motion (reflection), $\\mathcal{P}$ and $\\mathcal{Q}$ must be congruent." :tutorial/id #uuid "511ff35e-2666-5989-ad2f-e3e9fe541c7c" :tutorial/math-academy-id 6163 :tutorial/title "Properties of Rigid Motions"} :step/id #uuid "1b767960-73f6-5f1a-86d5-06e3a151b4d8" :step/math-academy-id 37367 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186135008}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186135006 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186135021 :tutorial/content "A **rigid motion** is any transformation that does not change the distances and angles between points. Rigid motions are also called **isometries**.\n\nThere are *only three* types of rigid motions:\n\n- Translations\n- Rotations\n- Reflections\n\n**Watch out!** The following types of transformations are *not* rigid motions:\n\n- Dilations\n- Stretches" :tutorial/id #uuid "9208af14-0cfd-5ca9-989f-3bf18330cf12" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2294 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "66e47972-9ac9-5e15-abc6-6b2f033b161a" :step/math-academy-id 9555 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134894}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186135007 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133976 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133546 :question/id #uuid "25f331e5-db8f-58bd-a4a6-24d7ed09db10" :question/math-academy-id "e-2906"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "811ba45c-7467-5cef-9fb8-a8282891b607" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134180} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134469}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Rigid Motions"} :step/id #uuid "43999184-e956-5a86-8726-8697e9473d18" :step/math-academy-id 9556} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186135008 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133977 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133547 :question/id #uuid "46db11d7-8448-54f5-a5ea-46abfc746574" :question/math-academy-id "e-2907"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cfe2598e-57bd-53fb-8477-9c4c5a8d3fa4" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048906} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051041}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134461} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134463}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Polygons That Map to Each Other Under Rigid Motions"} :step/id #uuid "21aa14a0-3abb-5d4a-92b6-d08d24876eb6" :step/math-academy-id 9558 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186135009}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186135009 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133978 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133548 :question/id #uuid "d928641d-fd70-5cbb-a217-e9e454a8bd51" :question/math-academy-id "e-2909"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e4ffa315-2f50-51da-a928-329e1816706f" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134079} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134464}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Why Polygons Are Congruent Using Rigid Motions"} :step/id #uuid "971e2526-fd20-58e6-bc97-09ccc8b2617e" :step/math-academy-id 9562 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186135010}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186135010 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133979 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133549 :question/id #uuid "5fb05996-774b-5a89-9cc1-6876cc60338e" :question/math-academy-id "e-2912"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b01281fd-5272-579c-98d5-ca5cc00c73e4" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048208} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049034} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050093} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050239}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134457} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134468} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234059} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234060}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Maps Presented in Function Notation That Are Rigid Motions"} :step/id #uuid "a91d4728-a024-5878-9599-76838230c6ed" :step/math-academy-id 9567 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134893}}] :activity/title "Rigid Motions and Congruence" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186134053}]}
